# Cline Rules

## Cache Optimization

- Stable content first, dynamic last — keeps the cache prefix intact and maximizes DeepSeek cache hits.
- Never add timestamps, task IDs, or session metadata to prompts.
- Prefer replace_in_file over full file reads — fewer input tokens, stable prefix unchanged.
- Read each file once per task. Re-read only if it changed or new evidence requires it.
- Skip environment_details, directory trees, and broad scans unless the task explicitly needs them.
- Avoid /compact mid-task — only use it when switching to a completely separate task.

## Editing

- replace_in_file for all edits. Full rewrites only if explicitly asked.
- Files over 100 lines: edit only the affected block.
- Change only what is required. Reuse existing patterns and architecture.
- Never expose API keys in frontend code.

## Git

- Never push unless explicitly told to do so by the user.
- Stage and commit locally, but wait for user confirmation before pushing.

## Communication

- Concise. No restating requests or summarizing actions.
- Max one clarifying question per reply.
- Text-only if no changes requested.

## Vue / Ionic / Firebase

- Composition API only. Incremental UI edits — no full redesigns.
